        "Start with an order brief, not a shopping link",
        "Many failed agent purchases begin with an incomplete instruction. A buyer pastes a link, assumes the listing explains everything, and notices the ambiguity only after the agent has paid the seller. Changing a color, size, bundle, logo option, or accessory can then require cancellation, seller approval, or a domestic return.\n\nTreat every Sugargoo purchase as a small order brief. Before paying, record the product name, seller, selected variation, quantity, visible price, domestic shipping charge, and any detail that would make the item unacceptable. Save a screenshot of the listing and chosen option because pages can change or disappear.\n\nSugargoo’s current official flow starts with pasting a Taobao, Tmall, or 1688 link, selecting size, color, and quantity, then paying for the order. The agent confirms the request with the seller and buys on the customer’s behalf. That process is efficient when the page loads correctly. Your responsibility is to make the handoff unambiguous before purchasing begins."
      ],
